(990905, 117180, 16004, '<td valign="top">for the first time in 429 comments, i am going to use the word "sexy" (i''ve yet to comment on any of my own photos of my other half).  your model is gorgeous, and you''ve captured her gorgeousness very nicely indeed.  the fur clothing, the wooden floor, posture, composition (even though i don''t normally like upside down type poses), facial expression, discreet glimpses of skin and everything else makes this a sensual and flirtatious image.  lovely - 10.</td>', 'for the first time in 429 comments, i am going to use the word "sexy" (i''ve yet to comment on any of my own photos of my other half).  your model is gorgeous, and you''ve captured her gorgeousness very nicely indeed.  the fur clothing, the wooden floor, posture, composition (even though i don''t normally like upside down type poses), facial expression, discreet glimpses of skin and everything else makes this a sensual and flirtatious image.  lovely - 10.', '2004-11-04 05:34:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(990908, 115117, 15832, '<td valign="top">This is amazing picture!! If there is anything i would have to say it´s maby just the sky.<br/>It lokks really cool but if i look closer the dots after the doging and burning are bothering me just a littel bit.<br/>8</td>', 'This is amazing picture!! If there is anything i would have to say it´s maby just the sky.It lokks really cool but if i look closer the dots after the doging and burning are bothering me just a littel bit.8', '2004-11-04 05:38:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(990909, 114045, 16004, '<td valign="top">very lovely autumnal colours here.  i''m not sure that the reflections in the water really adds very much - i think it''s becoming slowly a bit of a cliche on this site...  and one personal gripe is showing everything that''s reflected.  Having the water edge along the middle of the photo just looks a bit unnatural.  Try cropping out the reflected sky, it might balance your image a bit and give a presentation in line with the rule of thirds, which really does work in terms of maximising visual appeal.  the tree is beautiful (so red!) and the yellow and orange bushes very pretty too.   6.</td>', 'very lovely autumnal colours here.  i''m not sure that the reflections in the water really adds very much - i think it''s becoming slowly a bit of a cliche on this site...  and one personal gripe is showing everything that''s reflected.  Having the water edge along the middle of the photo just looks a bit unnatural.  Try cropping out the reflected sky, it might balance your image a bit and give a presentation in line with the rule of thirds, which really does work in terms of maximising visual appeal.  the tree is beautiful (so red!) and the yellow and orange bushes very pretty too.   6.', '2004-11-04 05:42:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(990910, 109332, 15832, '<td valign="top">How did you do that?<br/>Abstract in a way..  If that´s not a photo of a photo, you creadit a art. Really nice 9</td>', 'How did you do that?Abstract in a way..  If that´s not a photo of a photo, you creadit a art. Really nice 9', '2004-11-04 05:43:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(990912, 117316, 15832, '<td valign="top">Excellent cropping.</td>', 'Excellent cropping.', '2004-11-04 05:45:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(990913, 116643, 15832, '<td valign="top">Cute.. This one is gonna get far in this challenge. Professonial work, Great momment captured 9</td>', 'Cute.. This one is gonna get far in this challenge. Professonial work, Great momment captured 9', '2004-11-04 05:47:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(990914, 117176, 6458, '<td valign="top">Too much foreground, not enough interest. Moving closer to the road on the left and making that more of a dominant element in your photograph would help the viewer.. use it as a leading line, not just as a secondary thought. Other than that, the exposure and details of this photo are very good.</td>', 'Too much foreground, not enough interest. Moving closer to the road on the left and making that more of a dominant element in your photograph would help the viewer.. use it as a leading line, not just as a secondary thought. Other than that, the exposure and details of this photo are very good.', '2004-11-04 05:50:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(990915, 111583, 16004, '<td valign="top">i like the angle that this has been taken very much - it''s very dramatic and it certainly conveys your title.  i might have been tempted to de-blue the sky, i.e. make it all B&amp;W or sepia even.  don''t know why, specifically, but i think it might work.  maybe, notwithstanding that the sky is also (beautifully) dramatic, the blueness feels a bit optimistic?  still, the shot DOES convey a lot of drama, got me thinking (breifly) about the merits (cool icons and flags) and disadvantages (Trabants and the KGB) of communism, and is enjoyable to view.  8.</td>', 'i like the angle that this has been taken very much - it''s very dramatic and it certainly conveys your title.  i might have been tempted to de-blue the sky, i.e. make it all B&W or sepia even.  don''t know why, specifically, but i think it might work.  maybe, notwithstanding that the sky is also (beautifully) dramatic, the blueness feels a bit optimistic?  still, the shot DOES convey a lot of drama, got me thinking (breifly) about the merits (cool icons and flags) and disadvantages (Trabants and the KGB) of communism, and is enjoyable to view.  8.', '2004-11-04 05:51:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(990917, 115678, 6458, '<td valign="top">Just a bit too saturated for my tastes, but I love the the scenery and the mountains, Especially in the distance. The hints of colour there are perfect... 8</td>', 'Just a bit too saturated for my tastes, but I love the the scenery and the mountains, Especially in the distance. The hints of colour there are perfect... 8', '2004-11-04 05:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(990919, 116815, 23251, '<td valign="top">Its a lovely scene but I don''t like the 2 trees on the right hand side, maybe a slightly differet angle or tighter crop.</td>', 'Its a lovely scene but I don''t like the 2 trees on the right hand side, maybe a slightly differet angle or tighter crop.', '2004-11-04 06:00:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(990920, 117214, 15832, '<td valign="top">Nice... This picture has a spiruatal atmosphere.. Good work. What i´ve seen so far the Cannon is the only one that can get those colors and dof like on the trees.<br/>Hope i´m wrong ;) 8</td>', 'Nice... This picture has a spiruatal atmosphere.. Good work. What i´ve seen so far the Cannon is the only one that can get those colors and dof like on the trees.Hope i´m wrong ;) 8', '2004-11-04 06:01:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(990921, 116629, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is one of the hardest pictures to comment on.  it''s unique feature which i do like is the inclusion of the Plough constellation.  i''ve never seen a such a thing so well defined in a photo before.  i think it''s a bit unbalanced by the area of black in the foreground, and i also think that the lighthouse seems a little small / lost in the shot.  it''s like, you''ve got two great things (three including the sunset) and you''re not sure which one you want us to look at.  i think thats the problem - there''s too much unrelated stuff in the shot.  less would be more, i think...  4.</td>', 'this is one of the hardest pictures to comment on.  it''s unique feature which i do like is the inclusion of the Plough constellation.  i''ve never seen a such a thing so well defined in a photo before.  i think it''s a bit unbalanced by the area of black in the foreground, and i also think that the lighthouse seems a little small / lost in the shot.  it''s like, you''ve got two great things (three including the sunset) and you''re not sure which one you want us to look at.  i think thats the problem - there''s too much unrelated stuff in the shot.  less would be more, i think...  4.', '2004-11-04 06:01:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(990922, 114806, 22781, '<td valign="top">Great clouds, I would like to see this in color</td>', 'Great clouds, I would like to see this in color', '2004-11-04 06:05:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(990923, 113523, 16004, '<td valign="top">i think i might be prepared to guess who this is, Mr Alci.  even if i''m wrong, it certainly has that very particular style which for bodily pictures works very well.  i love the tones you''ve used (not quite sepia, kind of green aren''t they?) and as per the norm, it all works very well.  the only slight criticism is that it appears a slightly over liberal use of neatimage (or similar) has been applied in the region of the hand.  still, a very dramatic, tense and attention grabbing shot.  8.</td>', 'i think i might be prepared to guess who this is, Mr Alci.  even if i''m wrong, it certainly has that very particular style which for bodily pictures works very well.  i love the tones you''ve used (not quite sepia, kind of green aren''t they?) and as per the norm, it all works very well.  the only slight criticism is that it appears a slightly over liberal use of neatimage (or similar) has been applied in the region of the hand.  still, a very dramatic, tense and attention grabbing shot.  8.', '2004-11-04 06:11:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(990924, 117115, 9073, '<td valign="top">The subject and treatment are fantastic. I''d prefer a touch more black to give the high key a touch more punch. 9</td>', 'The subject and treatment are fantastic. I''d prefer a touch more black to give the high key a touch more punch. 9', '2004-11-04 06:13:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(990926, 117209, 15832, '<td valign="top">Thats a funny idea... Nice colors there. I don´t know why but i would have liked to see her neck there aswell. Not croped so tight at the buttom. 7</td>', 'Thats a funny idea... Nice colors there. I don´t know why but i would have liked to see her neck there aswell. Not croped so tight at the buttom. 7', '2004-11-04 06:24:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(990927, 117079, 16004, '<td valign="top">...a picture of loveliness!  very nice classic portrait.  things i like: depth of field, smile, details of the eyes.  things i don''t like:  erm, none of it!  it''s not a deeply original shot, but what it is is very well done and nice and sunny.  8.</td>', '...a picture of loveliness!  very nice classic portrait.  things i like: depth of field, smile, details of the eyes.  things i don''t like:  erm, none of it!  it''s not a deeply original shot, but what it is is very well done and nice and sunny.  8.', '2004-11-04 06:25:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(990934, 110954, 25355, '<td valign="top">way too small</td>', 'way too small', '2004-11-04 06:36:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(990936, 117085, 15832, '<td valign="top">That´s a dramatic momment captured there. I would have liked to see the people just a littel bit closer to the camera( still not sure) but anyway, that picture is gonna get far in this challenge. topp 10. Good use of burning. 9</td>', 'That´s a dramatic momment captured there. I would have liked to see the people just a littel bit closer to the camera( still not sure) but anyway, that picture is gonna get far in this challenge. topp 10. Good use of burning. 9', '2004-11-04 06:41:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(990937, 115932, 16004, '<td valign="top">conceptually, this is a wonderful image.  the colours are striking, quite surreal and very dramatic.  the guy doesn''t detract from the overall effect, though i think it would help if he was a little better defined.  the glow of the lights and the angle of the shot are also excellent.  it feels a little bit strange though - for example, the brickwork on the brdge doesn''t look quite right (perhaps it''s the result of over processing / editting?)  this is still incredibly likeable.  9.</td>', 'conceptually, this is a wonderful image.  the colours are striking, quite surreal and very dramatic.  the guy doesn''t detract from the overall effect, though i think it would help if he was a little better defined.  the glow of the lights and the angle of the shot are also excellent.  it feels a little bit strange though - for example, the brickwork on the brdge doesn''t look quite right (perhaps it''s the result of over processing / editting?)  this is still incredibly likeable.  9.', '2004-11-04 06:42:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(990940, 116643, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is a great picture, full of humour and life.  the pose feels very genuine and natural.  the brightness of the image also works strikingly well.  i can''t comment too much on this because it''s great, and i can''t think of a single way to improve it.  a lovely, sweet, family shot.  hopefully will finish in the top 10.  gets an easy 10 from me, anyway.</td>', 'this is a great picture, full of humour and life.  the pose feels very genuine and natural.  the brightness of the image also works strikingly well.  i can''t comment too much on this because it''s great, and i can''t think of a single way to improve it.  a lovely, sweet, family shot.  hopefully will finish in the top 10.  gets an easy 10 from me, anyway.', '2004-11-04 06:45:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(990943, 112981, 9073, '<td valign="top">This makes me laugh. The eye line, the flayed nose, the lips. I think that you could have brought out the humour a bit more through careful cropping.</td>', 'This makes me laugh. The eye line, the flayed nose, the lips. I think that you could have brought out the humour a bit more through careful cropping.', '2004-11-04 06:50:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(990947, 116696, 1368, '<td valign="top">Great colors and composition The expression on their face is amazing I love it :)</td>', 'Great colors and composition The expression on their face is amazing I love it :)', '2004-11-04 06:54:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(990948, 117253, 16004, '<td valign="top">the posing of this shot and the capturing of the couple is very natural in feel and happy in spirit.  The only thing that slightly diminishes the overall shot is the low levels of light.  the dull coloured buildings behind the trees are partly to blame, but this might have been rectified with a bit of post editting and brightness adjustment.  this is still a great wedding photo - so much better than most of the stilted shots you normally see.  the girls facial expression is priceless!  7.</td>', 'the posing of this shot and the capturing of the couple is very natural in feel and happy in spirit.  The only thing that slightly diminishes the overall shot is the low levels of light.  the dull coloured buildings behind the trees are partly to blame, but this might have been rectified with a bit of post editting and brightness adjustment.  this is still a great wedding photo - so much better than most of the stilted shots you normally see.  the girls facial expression is priceless!  7.', '2004-11-04 06:56:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(990954, 115482, 16004, '<td valign="top">FANTISSIMO!!  colours are so exotically gorgeous.  the landscape is so so dramatically dramatic.  i can''t decide if i would have cropped just below the light blue sky though...  no i like the mountains being defined.  this is a great shot - only slight criticism is that it looks almost too perfect (the rich blue behind the golden sand looks too superb).  this is a great landscape picture.  10.</td>', 'FANTISSIMO!!  colours are so exotically gorgeous.  the landscape is so so dramatically dramatic.  i can''t decide if i would have cropped just below the light blue sky though...  no i like the mountains being defined.  this is a great shot - only slight criticism is that it looks almost too perfect (the rich blue behind the golden sand looks too superb).  this is a great landscape picture.  10.', '2004-11-04 07:10:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(990957, 114038, 16004, '<td valign="top">it''s a good silhouette type picture, but for me, isn''t too exciting.  i think the quantity of bushes etc is a little overpowering, and i think that maybe the sky could do with a bit of emphasising enhancing the dark and light areas (if you have Photoshop, try using curves, failing that play with brightness and contrast of the sky in whatever software you have got).   4.</td>', 'it''s a good silhouette type picture, but for me, isn''t too exciting.  i think the quantity of bushes etc is a little overpowering, and i think that maybe the sky could do with a bit of emphasising enhancing the dark and light areas (if you have Photoshop, try using curves, failing that play with brightness and contrast of the sky in whatever software you have got).   4.', '2004-11-04 07:16:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(990958, 117147, 18191, '<td valign="top">Good choice of shutter speed to give this a cool, flowing effect. One bit of a suggestion is to place the waterfall more to the right or left of the frame in order to compose it. This would call for a reshoot of the area, but would also improve the image tremendously.</td>', 'Good choice of shutter speed to give this a cool, flowing effect. One bit of a suggestion is to place the waterfall more to the right or left of the frame in order to compose it. This would call for a reshoot of the area, but would also improve the image tremendously.', '2004-11-04 07:16:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(990960, 116959, 18191, '<td valign="top">Nice lighting that is not too harsh...it helps to separate the subject from the background. Very good detail as well. Not to candy coat everything, but it is technically right-on, but the subject matter is a little bit uninteresting. I still set this apart from some of the other middle of the road fall leaf photographs. Good job.</td>', 'Nice lighting that is not too harsh...it helps to separate the subject from the background. Very good detail as well. Not to candy coat everything, but it is technically right-on, but the subject matter is a little bit uninteresting. I still set this apart from some of the other middle of the road fall leaf photographs. Good job.', '2004-11-04 07:17:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(990962, 117196, 19009, '<td valign="top">Nice shot.almost could have cropped out the handle for a change in composition.</td>', 'Nice shot.almost could have cropped out the handle for a change in composition.', '2004-11-04 07:20:10.000000', NULL, 1),
