(990970, 110954, 16004, '<td valign="top">i''m sure 90% of comments refer in some way to the size of the picture, and yes, it is a serious issue.  the picture shows an awful lot of promise - tall trees, rolling cloud and mountains always look good.  but not when squinting at the screen.  if the reason for the size was a 150kb issue, try a lower quality setting (most have microsoft photo editor - when save as click the more button and you can adjust quality there).  7 (because i can see this would have been a stormer).</td>', 'i''m sure 90% of comments refer in some way to the size of the picture, and yes, it is a serious issue.  the picture shows an awful lot of promise - tall trees, rolling cloud and mountains always look good.  but not when squinting at the screen.  if the reason for the size was a 150kb issue, try a lower quality setting (most have microsoft photo editor - when save as click the more button and you can adjust quality there).  7 (because i can see this would have been a stormer).', '2004-11-04 07:22:54.000000', NULL, 1),
