(991812, 114082, 19943, '<td valign="top">OK, I like it because of the eerie feel, but the subject (old barn) is not very interesting to look at.....</td>', 'OK, I like it because of the eerie feel, but the subject (old barn) is not very interesting to look at.....', '2004-11-04 14:48:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(991817, 114797, 22781, '<td valign="top">You call this picture grand morning and that just askes for a comment.<br/>Seeing the shadows I would say it is almost midday, as you know the most beautifull light is in the early morning (sunrise or just after) or the late afternoon (just before or at sunset) I think the photo could have been more exeptional when taken in the right light. Now it looks just a lttle flat and the haze takes away from the background.<br/> <br/>Another thing that you could have done is this (little trick)<br/>Open up the photo in Photoshop press: ctrl alt ~ (three keys at one time)<br/>It will select the lightness, then goto image-&gt;adjustments-&gt;Brightness/contrast and "up" the contrast around 40% then goto select -&gt; Deselect and look at you picture again.<br/> <br/>I hope you vote this comment helpfull :) Good luck!</td>', 'You call this picture grand morning and that just askes for a comment.Seeing the shadows I would say it is almost midday, as you know the most beautifull light is in the early morning (sunrise or just after) or the late afternoon (just before or at sunset) I think the photo could have been more exeptional when taken in the right light. Now it looks just a lttle flat and the haze takes away from the background. Another thing that you could have done is this (little trick)Open up the photo in Photoshop press: ctrl alt ~ (three keys at one time)It will select the lightness, then goto image->adjustments->Brightness/contrast and "up" the contrast around 40% then goto select -> Deselect and look at you picture again. I hope you vote this comment helpfull :) Good luck!', '2004-11-04 14:49:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(991820, 117060, 22781, '<td valign="top">Very saturated. just a bit too much for my taste...<br/>But I like the composition AND the color in the sky..</td>', 'Very saturated. just a bit too much for my taste...But I like the composition AND the color in the sky..', '2004-11-04 14:50:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(991823, 117126, 22781, '<td valign="top">What is this I am looking at, it looks nice but also a bit disturbing...<br/>Looks almost like an alien... What is it? Foam? What is it used for?<br/>Questions questions questions :)</td>', 'What is this I am looking at, it looks nice but also a bit disturbing...Looks almost like an alien... What is it? Foam? What is it used for?Questions questions questions :)', '2004-11-04 14:51:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(991826, 117228, 22781, '<td valign="top">Could have used a little USM and just a litlle bit more saturation to realy bring out the color..</td>', 'Could have used a little USM and just a litlle bit more saturation to realy bring out the color..', '2004-11-04 14:53:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(991829, 115199, 25143, '<td valign="top">clear winner ... swimming in golden colors tinted with green -  gorgeous!!!</td>', 'clear winner ... swimming in golden colors tinted with green -  gorgeous!!!', '2004-11-04 14:55:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(991831, 117051, 22781, '<td valign="top">Could have done with some (more) usm to make it nice and crisp.<br/>Another thing that you could have done is this (little trick)<br/>Open up the photo in Photoshop press: ctrl alt ~ (three keys at one time)<br/>It will select the lightness, then goto image-&gt;adjustments-&gt;Brightness/contrast and "up" the contrast around 40% then goto select -&gt; Deselect and look at you picture again.<br/>It gives the picture some more color without making everything oversaturated and making it a bit more believable...<br/> <br/>Still a nice picture, good luck.<br/></td>', 'Could have done with some (more) usm to make it nice and crisp.Another thing that you could have done is this (little trick)Open up the photo in Photoshop press: ctrl alt ~ (three keys at one time)It will select the lightness, then goto image->adjustments->Brightness/contrast and "up" the contrast around 40% then goto select -> Deselect and look at you picture again.It gives the picture some more color without making everything oversaturated and making it a bit more believable... Still a nice picture, good luck.', '2004-11-04 14:56:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(991832, 110125, 22781, '<td valign="top">It looks a bit flat (because of the overcast sky.<br/>Could have done with some (more) usm to make it nice and crisp.<br/>Another thing that you could have done is this (little trick)<br/>Open up the photo in Photoshop press: ctrl alt ~ (three keys at one time)<br/>It will select the lightness, then goto image-&gt;adjustments-&gt;Brightness/contrast and "up" the contrast around 40% then goto select -&gt; Deselect and look at you picture again.<br/>It gives the picture some more color without making everything oversaturated and making it a bit more believable...<br/> <br/>Still a nice picture, good luck.<br/></td>', 'It looks a bit flat (because of the overcast sky.Could have done with some (more) usm to make it nice and crisp.Another thing that you could have done is this (little trick)Open up the photo in Photoshop press: ctrl alt ~ (three keys at one time)It will select the lightness, then goto image->adjustments->Brightness/contrast and "up" the contrast around 40% then goto select -> Deselect and look at you picture again.It gives the picture some more color without making everything oversaturated and making it a bit more believable... Still a nice picture, good luck.', '2004-11-04 14:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
