(997689, 114842, 19982, '<td valign="top">One thing I like to do before I use USM, especially wth lots of tiny details (like leaves, branches, grass) that are not part of the subject, is this:  Mask around the subject so that the main thing that gets sharpened is the subject.  That way the uninteresting details don''t get sharpened.  I think this image could benefit from that.  It appears that USM oversharpened the grass.  The girls is PERFECT however!  Good luck in the challenge!<br/></td>', 'One thing I like to do before I use USM, especially wth lots of tiny details (like leaves, branches, grass) that are not part of the subject, is this:  Mask around the subject so that the main thing that gets sharpened is the subject.  That way the uninteresting details don''t get sharpened.  I think this image could benefit from that.  It appears that USM oversharpened the grass.  The girls is PERFECT however!  Good luck in the challenge!', '2004-11-07 21:10:49.000000', NULL, 1),
