(998463, 116820, 8860, '<td valign="top">I hate to spoil the party here (which I probably won''t), but I think you''re mighty lucky that this is no. 2 or even in the top 20! While a nice scene this is transparently over processed to the point of confusion. There really is a massive imbalance in the sky related to the ground so that they look divorced from each other.<br/> <br/>Seems to me that this kind of editing is in vogue here now but it''s not the photo that''s winning for you here but Photoshop edits that appeal to gimmick fans (despite starting out with a healthy shot). I like your other work but this is a step in the wrong direction despite the result. <br/> <br/>No offence intended, just a [strong] opinion on this kind of stuff.</td>', 'I hate to spoil the party here (which I probably won''t), but I think you''re mighty lucky that this is no. 2 or even in the top 20! While a nice scene this is transparently over processed to the point of confusion. There really is a massive imbalance in the sky related to the ground so that they look divorced from each other. Seems to me that this kind of editing is in vogue here now but it''s not the photo that''s winning for you here but Photoshop edits that appeal to gimmick fans (despite starting out with a healthy shot). I like your other work but this is a step in the wrong direction despite the result.  No offence intended, just a [strong] opinion on this kind of stuff.', '2004-11-08 06:33:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(998468, 111575, 21069, '<td valign="top">The problem with your photo is not the water, its perfect but the surroundings are not -its crap- The surrounding have no feeling of depth so your picture looks very flat<br/> <br/>no real details in the leaves or rocks - I think if you jst had it cropped or reshoot &lt;more of the water&gt; - bigger of course you would of ranked higher<br/> <br/>The viewer wants to be placed within the image and feel like the water is gushing out of the screen onto them - but not to the intent of drowning them, more like having the feeling of being a person standing on the water edge with the water flowing by, quietly and peacefully<br/> <br/>anyway this is how I feel a picture of waterfalls should be portrayed + more moss would of made it alot nicer<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-08 07:00:43.</i></td>', 'The problem with your photo is not the water, its perfect but the surroundings are not -its crap- The surrounding have no feeling of depth so your picture looks very flat no real details in the leaves or rocks - I think if you jst had it cropped or reshoot <more of the water> - bigger of course you would of ranked higher The viewer wants to be placed within the image and feel like the water is gushing out of the screen onto them - but not to the intent of drowning them, more like having the feeling of being a person standing on the water edge with the water flowing by, quietly and peacefully anyway this is how I feel a picture of waterfalls should be portrayed + more moss would of made it alot nicer', '2004-11-08 06:43:53.000000', '2004-11-08 07:00:43.000000', 0),
