(999672, 117207, 7778, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for taking the time to say something about this image.<br/> <br/>To those who were (and to those who, apparently, still are) concerned with a photo crossing the line into digital art: <br/> <br/>The shot was a tripod-mounted, remote-released capture at a 500 mm focal length. At this focal length a strong bokeh is what can be expected. Yes, I did apply Smart Blur to further emphasize the existing bokeh and to isolate the crow. That''s the full extent of extravagance afforded this image.<br/> <br/>The title, by the way, illustrates the ways of crows. Since both the phrase and the attribution are Mark Twain''s I expected it would ring familiar to American ears especially.<br/>I also felt it was a title which reflected some signs of the times. ;-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-08 20:45:56.</i></td>', 'Thanks everyone for taking the time to say something about this image. To those who were (and to those who, apparently, still are) concerned with a photo crossing the line into digital art:  The shot was a tripod-mounted, remote-released capture at a 500 mm focal length. At this focal length a strong bokeh is what can be expected. Yes, I did apply Smart Blur to further emphasize the existing bokeh and to isolate the crow. That''s the full extent of extravagance afforded this image. The title, by the way, illustrates the ways of crows. Since both the phrase and the attribution are Mark Twain''s I expected it would ring familiar to American ears especially.I also felt it was a title which reflected some signs of the times. ;-)', '2004-11-08 18:47:21.000000', '2004-11-08 20:45:56.000000', 0),
(999678, 109332, 20066, '<td valign="top">I think this one is far too artistic to get the voting it deserves (that is higher than it got)</td>', 'I think this one is far too artistic to get the voting it deserves (that is higher than it got)', '2004-11-08 18:52:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(999697, 113451, 22975, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by e301:</b></div><hr/><i> IR now ... I think it depends for so much of its impact on never having seen it before, and for me I don''t find enough other interrest here: the composition is strong, effective, and the quality of light you''ve caught is nice, but not really a winner for me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You know... I''m sorry you don''t like my IR shot because it''s not the first time you''ve ever seen it, but it''s the first time I''ve ever done it, and I don''t think it''s fair to vote down something by comparing it to something you''ve seen before.  How many ideas on here are really original anyway?</td>', 'Originally posted by e301: IR now ... I think it depends for so much of its impact on never having seen it before, and for me I don''t find enough other interrest here: the composition is strong, effective, and the quality of light you''ve caught is nice, but not really a winner for me.   You know... I''m sorry you don''t like my IR shot because it''s not the first time you''ve ever seen it, but it''s the first time I''ve ever done it, and I don''t think it''s fair to vote down something by comparing it to something you''ve seen before.  How many ideas on here are really original anyway?', '2004-11-08 19:06:01.000000', NULL, 0),
