(999999, 116791, 2344, '<td valign="top">Thank you all so much for all the wonderful comments. I really enjoyed this challenge and reading all the nice things people have to say about my picture. This photo was taken as a part of a session I did for my friend''s mother. One of my first paid sessions... so I''m quite excited about it<br/> <br/>Thanks a lot guys!</td>', 'Thank you all so much for all the wonderful comments. I really enjoyed this challenge and reading all the nice things people have to say about my picture. This photo was taken as a part of a session I did for my friend''s mother. One of my first paid sessions... so I''m quite excited about it Thanks a lot guys!', '2004-11-08 21:20:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1000037, 117150, 22140, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tfaust:</b></div><hr/><i> Speaking on title alone, this image doesn''t speak ''Autumn'' to me at all.  Speaking of the photo in general, I don''t see much that captures my interest. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well thanks...That''s constructive.  Given your stated lack of interest, you could have withheld comment...<br/> <br/>So you know, autumn is alliterative and refers to the timing of enlightenment.  I live in Hawaii which looks this way all year round (not too much in the way of color changes).</td>', 'Originally posted by tfaust: Speaking on title alone, this image doesn''t speak ''Autumn'' to me at all.  Speaking of the photo in general, I don''t see much that captures my interest.   Well thanks...That''s constructive.  Given your stated lack of interest, you could have withheld comment... So you know, autumn is alliterative and refers to the timing of enlightenment.  I live in Hawaii which looks this way all year round (not too much in the way of color changes).', '2004-11-08 21:44:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1000104, 115027, 16301, '<td valign="top">Excellent portrait, I just don''t know why it didn''t get a higher score! :)</td>', 'Excellent portrait, I just don''t know why it didn''t get a higher score! :)', '2004-11-08 22:43:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1000286, 117311, 5912, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone.  I''d love to have some more though.<br/> <br/>Why are bridges covered?<br/> <br/>What you''re really trying to protect in a covered bridge are the structural members--the trusses. Made of heavy timber, these are the expensive part of the bridge, and if they fall apart due to exposure to the elements, so does the bridge. An unprotected wooden bridge will last maybe ten years. Put a cover over it, however, and it''ll last for centuries.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone.  I''d love to have some more though. Why are bridges covered? What you''re really trying to protect in a covered bridge are the structural members--the trusses. Made of heavy timber, these are the expensive part of the bridge, and if they fall apart due to exposure to the elements, so does the bridge. An unprotected wooden bridge will last maybe ten years. Put a cover over it, however, and it''ll last for centuries.', '2004-11-09 02:00:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1000347, 115482, 11078, '<td valign="top">How you can get 2 ones for this I dont know!!<br/>I tried to vote but as I am moving home I only got around to about 170 images I didnt see this. 488 is so hard to vote on on Dial up <br/> <br/>This is beautiful and so crisp the colours amazing a well deserved Blue Ribbon Great work Congrats <br/></td>', 'How you can get 2 ones for this I dont know!!I tried to vote but as I am moving home I only got around to about 170 images I didnt see this. 488 is so hard to vote on on Dial up  This is beautiful and so crisp the colours amazing a well deserved Blue Ribbon Great work Congrats ', '2004-11-09 02:30:25.000000', NULL, 0),
